# =============================================================================
# VERCEL PRODUCTION — set these in the Vercel project dashboard (Environment Variables)
# Do NOT commit real secrets. Demo Vercel project should use a separate Neon DB.
# =============================================================================
#
# Architecture:
#   - Web (super admin): browser → same Vercel URL → /admin
#   - Mobile (owners/cashiers): Capacitor app → VITE_SAAS_API_URL (HTTPS, baked at build)
#   - API + SPA on one deployment (vercel.json rewrites /api/* → serverless function)
#
# Create prod project: Vercel → Add New Project → same Git repo → Production branch
# Connect Neon: Vercel Storage / Neon integration → sets SAAS_DATABASE_URL (use pooled URL)

# --- Required (Production + Preview) ---

# Neon PostgreSQL (pooled connection string recommended for serverless)
SAAS_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST/neondb?sslmode=require

# Random string, at least 32 characters (API exits on Vercel if weak/missing)
JWT_SECRET=

# Comma-separated. Must include your prod web URL + Capacitor WebView origins.
# Never use * on Vercel — startup will fail.
SAAS_CORS_ORIGINS=https://app.yourdomain.com,capacitor://localhost,ionic://localhost

# Platform super-admin login (comma-separated emails)
SUPER_ADMIN_EMAILS=you@yourcompany.com

# Frontend build (Vercel sets NODE_ENV=production automatically)
VITE_APP_MODE=saas

# Optional: leave unset on Vercel web — SPA uses same-origin /api when empty.
# Set only if you split API to another host (unusual for this repo).
# VITE_SAAS_API_URL=

# --- Optional ---

# Billing contact shown in payment instructions UI
# BILLING_GCASH=09XX XXX XXXX
# BILLING_BANK=BDO — …
# BILLING_CONTACT_PHONE=+63 …
# BILLING_CONTACT_EMAIL=hello@example.com

# --- After first deploy ---
# From your machine (once per prod Neon DB):
#   SAAS_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://..." npm run prisma:migrate:saas:prod
#
# Smoke test:
#   curl https://app.yourdomain.com/api/health
#
# Mobile Play Store build (local machine, not Vercel):
#   cp .env.saas-production .env.saas.local
#   # edit VITE_SAAS_API_URL=https://app.yourdomain.com
#   npm run build:mobile:saas:prod
